  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 122 PM MDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nVery warm temperatures still on tap for this afternoon, with\ncontinued expectations for a few locations nearing or exceeding\nrecord highs. Models heading into Monday still showing isolated\nconvection mainly across the southern highlands but a few storms\nstill possible across the central mountains as well. Moisture\nremains limited, so any storms that can develop are expected to\nbe dry with little precipitation. Gusty outflows will remain\npossible especially across the southern highlands. Upper ridge\nrebounds through the remainder of the work week, with\ntemperatures remaining unseasonably warm. We are still seeing\npotential for a trough to work into the region for next weekend.\nEnsemble means swing trough southeast into the PacNW by\nSaturday, but there is still quite a bit of variability in the\nclusters regarding depth and timing of the feature. QPf and\ntemperatures still remain uncertain at this time, but the NBM\nhas trended toward cooler and wetter for next weekend.",
